LOCATION:Fowler Student Center - Room 350
GEO:45.44918;-122.670969
SUMMARY:Managing Menopause: Expert Panel + Complimentary Lunch
DESCRIPTION:Everyone on campus interacts with people who are approaching\
 , in the middle of\, or have gone through menopause. And yet\, this topic
  is still very much taboo.&#160\;  L&amp\;C's Managing Menopause Employee
  Resource Group is hosting a panel discussion to learn from wellness expe
 rts\, share resources\, offer support\, and break down the stigma of disc
 ussing this topic.  All identities are welcome and encouraged to particip
 ate.Date: Monday\, May 18  Time: 11:30 a.m. to 1 p.m.  Location: Fowler 3
 50    Panelists include:Julie BrowningJulie Browning&#160\;  National Boa
 rd-Certified Health and Wellness Coach\; received training from Well Coac
 hes. Additional training in Lifestyle Medicine Coaching\, Group Health Co
 aching and Whole Food Plant-Based eating. Holds an undergraduate degree i
 n Physical Education.Susan HaralabatosSusan Haralabatos&#160\;  Board Cer
 tified Orthopedic Surgeon\, Degree is from the University of Colorado Uni
 versity of New Mexico. Fellowship and residency training at SUNY Stony Br
 ook. Additional training as a Certified Executive Coach. Founder of Prior
 ity Coaching and Consulting\, helping individuals achieve their personal 
 and professional goals  For more information\, please email Vanessa Holmg
 ren\, holmgren@lclark.edu (mailto:holmgren@lclark.edu)
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Everyone on campus interacts with peopl
 e who are approaching\, in the middle of\, or have gone through menopause
 . And yet\, this topic is still very much taboo.&#160\;</p><p>  L&amp\;C'
 s Managing Menopause Employee Resource Group is hosting a panel discussio
 n to learn from wellness experts\, share resources\, offer support\, and 
 break down the stigma of discussing this topic.</p><p>  All identities ar
 e welcome and encouraged to participate.</p><ul><li><strong>Date:</strong
 > Monday\, May 18  </li><li><strong>Time:</strong> 11:30 a.m. to 1 p.m.  
 </li><li><strong>Location:</strong> Fowler 350  </li></ul><h4>  Panelists
  include:</h4><h5><picture class="lw_image lw_image112988 lw_align_left">
