BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260709
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260710
LOCATION:Online
SUMMARY:Cultivating Spaciousness and Abundance: Courage to Lead® for Sus
 tainable Growth (Online)
DESCRIPTION:As leaders we are often called to come from a place of perpet
 ual productivity\, bottomless capacity\, always giving and always "on". Y
 et the wholeness of who we are requires periods of reflection\, receiving
  and renewal. When we do not honor this necessary balance\, the wisdom of
  our hearts is harder to hear.What's growing in your life? What needs to 
 be nourished for further growth? What do you want to prune or clear out?H
 ow do we listen to and honor what we need to be whole and in balance amid
  the demands and desires of an abundant life\, in a way that allows for s
 paciousness\, authenticity and joy?How do we tend to the garden of our li
 ves and our work so that we can receive what we need to flourish?  Held d
 uring a time of peak growth and seasonal abundance\, this Courage to Lead
 ® two-day workshop invites us into spacious time for reflection\, connec
 tion\, and inner growth.Together we will…      Pause and cultivate our 
 capacity to be present          Meaningfully engage with ourselves\, othe
 rs and nature with spaciousness and care          Take stock of our relat
 ionship to abundance and consider intentional paths of growth and clearin
 g          Develop skills for holding meaningful conversations and buildi
 ng relational trust          Explore reflective and creative practices in
 cluding the SoulCollage (https://soulcollage.com/about/)® method\, an ex
 pressive arts practice used as a tool for accessing personal and archetyp
 al wisdom      To ensure your SoulCollage (https://soulcollage.com/about/
 )® materials packet arrives before the workshop\, register by June 24.De
 tails &amp\; RegistrationDates and Times: Thursday-Friday\, July 9-10\, 2
 026\, 9:30 a.m.-2:30 p.m. PT\, OnlineFacilitators: Matsya Siosal\, and Ra
 faela Steen\, LCSWRegistration: $225. Includes 9 PDUs or CEUs\, and mater
 ials packetRegister Online (https://lclark.tfaforms.net/4735427?epid=a1aU
 Y000002Wikj)Scholarship Fund: We strive to keep our Courage retreats acce
 ssible to all who wish to participate. Please consider making a tax-deduc
 tible donation (https://engage.lclark.edu/register/gsecgiving?sys:gift:fu
 nd=4dfb9f4e-7351-4d84-91fe-531631c248c7&amp\;sys:gift:notes=Courage%20and
 %20Renewal%20Retreats%20Scholarship%20Fund) to our scholarship fund.Acces
 sibility: We are committed to making our events accessible to all needs a
 nd abilities. When registering\, please let us know your access needs. Co
 ntact us at 503-768-6040 or cce@lclark.edu (mailto:cce@lclark.edu)&#160\;
 with questions.Please note: Discounted &#x2018\;Student Rate&#x2019\; reg
 istrations are for current students only and do not include continuing ed
 ucation credit (CEU/PDUs)About the Facilitators Matsya Siosal has develop
 ed her skills in leadership and facilitation for over 25 years\, includin
 g roles with small and large for-profit corporations\, mission-driven con
 sumer goods companies\, higher education\, and as a consultant and entrep
 reneur. She has served as the director of the Center for Community Engage
 ment at Lewis &amp\; Clark since 2015\, after joining the department in 2
 010 to work in marketing and program management. Matsya is also co-founde
 r and managing partner of Sea-O-Salt Bath Company (http://www.seaosalt.co
 m/). Matsya is an experienced certified facilitator of Courage &amp\; Ren
 ewal programs. She has facilitated Circle of Trust\, Courage to Lead\, an
 d Leading Together workshops and retreats since 2019\, and is trained as 
 a SoulCollage® (https://soulcollage.com/) facilitator. As a facilitator 
 and coach\, Matsya supports mission-driven leaders in accessing their aut
 hentic voice\, and finding clarity and self-trust so they can show up wit
 h wholeheartedness and sustainability in their lives and work. Rafaela St
 een\, LCSW has been bringing people together for purpose\, support\, and 
 connection for most of her adult life. For the last two decades\, Rafaela
  has worked as an educational leader and strengths-based licensed clinica
 l social worker offering consultation\, guidance\, and professional devel
 opment related to mental health and well-being in K-12 schools and distri
 cts. Rafaela is an experienced facilitator\, thought partner\, convener\,
  and problem solver who sees the importance of meaningful connection and 
 joy within communities. Rafaela intentionally and strategically creates p
 roactive\, welcoming communities of care throughout her life\, both perso
 nally and professionally.New workshops and trainings are added to our cal
 endar regularly. For the latest on professional development related to yo
 ur specific interests\, sign up for our mailing list! (https://lclark.tfa
 forms.net/4735441)
