LOCATION:Online
SUMMARY:Strengthening Support for LGBTQ+ Students in Challenging Times (O
 nline)
DESCRIPTION:With changing and unstable politics\, policies\, and resource
 s\, knowing how to effectively support LGBTQ+ students has become increas
 ingly complicated for educators and adults.  This workshop for school-bas
 ed staff and administrators will ground into best practices in supporting
  LGBTQ+ students\, and will explore practices that can help bring these g
 uidelines into learning spaces.  This will include a review of Oregon's u
 pdated LGBTQ+ Student Success Plan (https://www.oregon.gov/ode/students-a
 nd-family/equity/lgbtq2siastudenteducation/pages/lgbtq2sia--student-succe
 ss-plan.aspx)\, and time spent generating ideas for creative\, innovative
 \, and responsive implementation of the included tools and recommendation
 s.  This workshop provides educators with an opportunity to connect with 
 other supportive adults across the state and address the real impact that
  the complicated political climate has had on each of us as educators\, c
 ommunity members\, and supportive adults. Ultimately\, this workshop will
  work to affirm educators as community change makers\, and reinforce the 
 concept of hope as an ongoing practice within our professions.Following t
 he workshop\, participants will be able to:Understand the use and modific
 ations of Oregon's LGBTQ+ Student Success Plan  Name two tools or approac
 hes that they can add to their practice as educators to increase student 
 inclusion at their school or workplace  Identify personal practices of ho
 pe that support their professional practice as a trusted adult for LGBTQ+
  students  Event Details &amp\; RegistrationDate and Time: Tuesday\, Augu
 st 4\, 2026\, 10 a.m-12 p.m.\, OnlineInstructor: Carson Varnum\, MEdRegis
 tration: $49\, includes 2 PDUs. GSEC Alumni and Adjuncts save 20%. $20 st
 udent rate.Current GSEC Supervisors\, Faculty and Staff: Free. Email cce@
 lclark.edu (mailto:cce@lclark.edu) to register.Register Online (https://l
 clark.tfaforms.net/wf1W4MQ?epid=a1aUY000002VSJp)Accessibility: We are com
 mitted to making our events accessible to all needs and abilities. When r
 egistering\, please let us know your access needs. Contact us at 503-768-
 6040 or cce@lclark.edu (mailto:cce@lclark.edu)&#160\;with questions.Pleas
 e note: Discounted &#x2018\;Student Rate&#x2019\; registrations are for c
 urrent students only and do not include continuing education credit (CEU/
 PDUs)About the InstructorCarson Varnum\, MEd\, (he/him) is a community bu
 ilder and educator with an expertise in sexual health\, sexualities\, pee
 r education\, and community development. Carson specializes in building c
 apacity in sex educators\, creating sexuality education and leadership de
 velopment programming for adolescents\, and developing programs that cent
 er Queer and Trans communities. Carson works at Lewis &amp\; Clark Gradua
 te School as TransActives's Head of Education and Outreach\, where he sup
 ports transgender\, non-binary\, and other gender expansive youth by stre
 ngthening the systems that surround them. He received his Masters of Educ
 ation in Human Sexuality from Widener University in 2012 and is currently
  a PhD student in Education and Leadership at Pacific University. Carson 
 is a big fan of being on mountains\, in rivers\, and with friends.&#160\;
 New workshops and trainings are added to our calendar regularly. For the 
 latest on professional development related to your specific interests\, s
 ign up for our mailing list! (https://lclark.tfaforms.net/4735441)
