  current students only and <strong>do not</strong> include continuing edu
 cation credit (CEU/PDUs)</em></p></div></li></ul></div><hr /><h2><strong>
 About the Instructor</strong></h2><p style="line-height: 1.5\;"><strong>S
 arah Weber\, MA\, LMHC\, LPC\, ATR</strong> (she/her) is an artist\, art 
 therapist\, and mental health counselor in Oregon and Washington states. 
 She works with folks of all ages who are living with anxiety disorders\, 
 OCD\, and trauma using both evidence-based practices (ACT\, ERP and I-CBT
 ) and expressive therapies. Sarah has worked in various settings\, from s
 chools to higher levels of care\, and is now in private practice. She is 
 on the board of OCD Washington and hosts art-making events to create comm
 unity. Outside of work\, she enjoys practicing yoga and spending time wit
 h her dog outdoors. Information about Sarah's practice <a href="http://ww
 w.sarah-weber.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">can be found here</a>.<
 /p><div id="lw_widget_470b39ba" class="lw_widget lw_widget_type_blurbs lw
