 p introduces clinicians to an integrative model of ketamine-assisted psyc
 hotherapy (KAP)\, an emerging treatment for trauma\, depression\, and oth
 er mental health conditions. Participants will explore KAP as a relationa
 l\, trauma-informed modality that facilitates access to implicit trauma m
 emories\, attachment patterns\, and internal parts often difficult to rea
 ch through traditional talk therapy.</p><p style="line-height: 1.5\;">  P
 articipants will learn how ketamine functions not as a standalone treatme
