  data-max-w="785" data-max-h="785" loading="lazy" data-optimized="true"/>
 </picture>Elizabeth Hoke\, LMFT</strong> is the Clinical Director of Libe
 ration Institute in Portland where she supervises and provides psychoeduc
 ational training and workshops. She specializes in working with addiction
  and trauma recovery\, using a mix of theoretical tools rooted in somatic
  psychology and Eastern philosophies. Elizabeth co-facilitates ketamine a
 ssisted psychotherapy sessions at Rainfall Medicine. She has completed th
 e 100-hour MDMA Therapy Training program through the Multidisciplinary As
 sociation for Psychedelic Studies and co-created the Entheogen Assisted P
 sychotherapy and Integration Training Series for licensed professionals a
 t Lewis &amp\; Clark college in the fall of 2021. Elizabeth is also a mem
 ber of Weaving Bridges Natural Fellowship and helped create a psilocybin 
 facilitator training program to teach individuals interested in becoming 
 psilocybin assisted facilitators licensed by the state of Oregon and is a
  psilocybin facilitator working with PNW Integrative Center.</p><p style=
 "line-height: 1.5\;"><strong><picture class="lw_image lw_image112919  lw_
 align_right"><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://www.lclark.edu/liv
