BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261024
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261025
LOCATION:Online
SUMMARY:Reconnecting with Voice and Purpose: A Full-Day Workshop for Educ
 ators (Online)
DESCRIPTION:As busy educators\, it can be difficult to stay attuned to ou
 r own voice amid the many demands and pressures of our work. This Circle 
 of Trust (https://couragerenewal.org/about-us/)® workshop\, grounded in 
 the writing of Parker J. Palmer and the Center for Courage &amp\; Renewal
 \, offers a space for caring and committed educators to slow down\, refle
 ct\, and listen deeply to themselves and one another. Together\, we will 
 reconnect with the meaning and purpose that nourish our lives as educator
 s.  During this full-day\, online workshop we will have the opportunity t
 o reflect in solitude and in community with other educators to:      Shar
 e stories of our life and work experiences          Remember the hopes an
 d dreams that brought us to our vocation&#160\;          Entertain possib
 ilities for the year ahead      We will turn to our own stories and exper
 iences\, those of others in the circle\, as well as insights from diverse
  creators of poetry\, art\, music\, and other visual media to help us con
 nect with ourselves and one another. Join us as we courageously navigate 
 the realities of education in these challenging times.Details &amp\; Regi
 strationDate and Time: Saturday\, October 24\, 2026\, 9 a.m.-4 p.m. PT\, 
 OnlineFacilitators: Dawn Montgomery\, EdD\; and Liza Finkel\, PhDRegistra
 tion: $135\, Includes 6 PDUs. Alumni save 20%Online Registration Coming S
 oonScholarship Fund:We strive to keep our Courage retreats accessible to 
 all who wish to participate. Please consider making atax-deductible donat
 ion (https://engage.lclark.edu/register/gsecgiving?sys:gift:fund=4dfb9f4e
 -7351-4d84-91fe-531631c248c7&amp\;sys:gift:notes=Courage%20and%20Renewal%
 20Retreats%20Scholarship%20Fund)to our scholarship fund.Accessibility: We
  are committed to making our events accessible to all needs and abilities
 . When registering\, please let us know your access needs. Contact us at 
 503-768-6040 or cce@lclark.edu (mailto:cce@lclark.edu)&#160\;with questio
 ns.Please note: Discounted &#x2018\;Student Rate&#x2019\; registrations a
 re for current students only and do not include continuing education cred
 it (CEU/PDUs)About the FacilitatorsLiza Finkel\, PhD is a teacher and tea
 cher educator with over 35 years of experience in middle\, high school\, 
 and post-secondary classrooms. She received her PhD in Science Education 
 at the University of Wisconsin-Madison and has worked with pre- and inser
 vice middle and high school teachers in schools across the U.S. Her past 
 leadership roles include Director of Field Experiences and Director of Te
 acher Education at the University of New Hampshire\; Senior Program Direc
 tor of the Center for Classroom Teaching and Learning at Education Northw
 est\; and Program Director of the Master of Arts in Teacher Education pro
 gram at the Graduate School of Education and Counseling at Lewis &amp\; C
 lark College in Portland\, OR. She has been trained as a Critical Friends
  Group Facilitator and has led Critical Friends Groups for teachers in al
 l areas and grade levels\, and is co-editor of the newly released book\, 
 Science Teaching for Social Justice\, published by Rethinking Schools. Li
 za is a certified Courage &amp\; Renewal facilitator who is passionate ab
 out working with teachers to create equitable and engaging learning situa
 tions for students\, and committed to supporting teachers to care for the
 mselves in ways that allow them to sustain their energy and commitment fo
 r the work of teaching.&#160\;Dawn Montgomery\, EdD is a change facilitat
 or and insightful thought partner. She supports leaders from a wide varie
 ty of fields\, including educators\, nonprofit executives\, and community
  administrators as they find their way in challenging times. Assisting hu
 mans in their discovery and reconnection to their deepest longings has be
 en a passion for many years. Her background in K-12 and college education
  as teacher\, principal\, and district leader support her coaching practi
 ce and team facilitation. She believes transformation is born when a circ
 le of humans sit together to listen\, to speak their deepest truths and t
 o share their wildest imaginations for the world. She is expert at holdin
 g space for both individual leaders and teams as an executive coach\, con
 flict mediator\, equity-focused professional developer and a certified Co
 urage &amp\; Renewal facilitator. She is committed to making a difference
  in the lives of individuals and their communities.&#160\;New workshops a
 nd trainings are added to our calendar regularly. For the latest on profe
 ssional development related to your specific interests\, sign up for our 
 mailing list! (https://lclark.tfaforms.net/4735441)
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p style="line-height: 1.5\;"><span style="b
 ackground-color: transparent\;">As busy educators\, it can be difficult t
 o stay attuned to our own voice amid the many demands and pressures of ou
 r work. This <a href="https://couragerenewal.org/about-us/" target="_blan
 k" rel="noopener">Circle of Trust</a>® workshop\, grounded in the writin
 g of Parker J. Palmer and the Center for Courage &amp\; Renewal\, offers 
 a space for caring and committed educators to slow down\, reflect\, and l
 isten deeply to themselves and one another. Together\, we will reconnect 
 with the meaning and purpose that nourish our lives as educators.</span><
 /p><h4 style="line-height: 1.5\;">  During this full-day\, online worksho
